apply. The vote page carries the voter and the tally, and the chaptered bill text carries the provision. Both are in `rests_on`, and the vote is in-term.\n- **Why rung 2:** Section 220.5(a) says schools and boards \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require\" staff to disclose a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches the rung's words.\n- **Why not rung 1:** the bill says staff \"shall not be required\" to disclose. It never requires them to keep the information from parents.\n- **The preemption question, which a reviewer may weigh differently:** this is a state law forbidding local school rules, which is the shape of the H12 preemption case. I did not treat it as `adjacent`, because rung 2 is itself about forbidding such rules, which is the exception V2 allows.\n- **Single-subject call:** I counted the bill as single-subject (pupil rights). Its parent-resources and anti-retaliation sections are on the same subject, so I didn't code it `multi-subject`.\n\n`needs_source` is empty and there are no candidate quotes.\n\nSeparately, the session reported that several connectors need authorization before they can be used: Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey and WorkOS. That is done in your claude.ai connector settings. The GitHub plugin server also failed to connect with a malformed-authorization error. None of them was needed for this task.","ttft_ms":12857,"type":"result","duration_ms":32257,"uuid":"8300f8f8-fee9-45a5-aae8-6ea4df55f4d3","ttft_stream_ms":1951,"time_to_request_ms":298,"first_content_frame_ms":1951,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
